From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:28:45 -0800
Subject: [MSE] Don't open a MediaSource whose context died mid-attachment

If the context owning a MediaSource (e.g. a same-origin iframe) is
destroyed after a media element in another document starts attaching
to it, but before the element's player opens its ChunkDemuxer, then
SameThreadMediaSourceAttachment::CompleteAttachingToMediaElement()
would still open the already-closed MediaSource and hand it a
WebMediaSource referencing the player's demuxer.

Since SameThreadMediaSourceAttachment::Close() skips closing a
MediaSource whose context is destroyed, nothing released that
WebMediaSource before the player destroyed the demuxer, so subsequent
MediaSource calls (e.g. reading duration) used the freed demuxer.

Like CrossThreadMediaSourceAttachment already does, skip completing
the attachment if the MediaSource's context has been destroyed.

Fixed: 577171064
Change-Id: I7bc07bda57cdda1454c7963430800b133ddbbb52
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8708355
Commit-Queue: Eugene Zemtsov <eugene@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Zemtsov <eugene@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1733536}

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/mediasource/same_thread_media_source_attachment.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/mediasource/same_thread_media_source_attachment.cc
index f70753785e3a0a35fe706de9f3a12e2701a7ad14..4fad83bc41cada63101502e69b9d50e9b51422ef 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/mediasource/same_thread_media_source_attachment.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/mediasource/same_thread_media_source_attachment.cc
@@ -251,6 +251,16 @@ SameThreadMediaSourceAttachment::StartAttachingToMediaElement(
 void SameThreadMediaSourceAttachment::CompleteAttachingToMediaElement(
     MediaSourceTracer* tracer,
     std::unique_ptr<WebMediaSource> web_media_source) {
+  // The MediaSource's context (e.g. a since-detached iframe) may have been
+  // destroyed after attachment started, but before the media element's player
+  // opened its demuxer. The MediaSource closed itself upon that context
+  // destruction, and Close() will not be called on it again, so it must not be
+  // opened now: nothing would then release |web_media_source| before the
+  // player destroys the demuxer which |web_media_source| references.
+  if (media_source_context_destroyed_) {
+    return;
+  }
+
   VerifyCalledWhileContextsAliveForDebugging();
 
   GetMediaSource(tracer)->CompleteAttachingToMediaElement(
diff --git a/third_party/blink/web_tests/http/tests/media/media-source/mediasource-iframe-detach-during-attach.html b/third_party/blink/web_tests/http/tests/media/media-source/mediasource-iframe-detach-during-attach.html
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ea328a3cd6f23bf9b1b51c835d497a2edb161a55
--- /dev/null
+++ b/third_party/blink/web_tests/http/tests/media/media-source/mediasource-iframe-detach-during-attach.html
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<title>Destroying a MediaSource's context during attachment keeps it closed</title>
+<script src="/w3c/resources/testharness.js"></script>
+<script src="/w3c/resources/testharnessreport.js"></script>
+<body>
+<script>
+// Regression test for https://crbug.com/577171064: when the context owning a
+// MediaSource is destroyed after a media element in another document starts
+// attaching to it, but before that attachment completes, the MediaSource must
+// remain closed. Otherwise it would open with a reference to the media
+// element's demuxer, which dangles once the element's player is destroyed.
+async_test(t => {
+  // The window load event is delayed until the media element finishes
+  // attaching to the MediaSource, so the test must start before load.
+  assert_equals(document.readyState, 'loading', 'document.readyState');
+
+  const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
+  document.body.appendChild(iframe);
+  const mediaSource = new iframe.contentWindow.MediaSource();
+
+  const video = document.createElement('video');
+  document.body.appendChild(video);
+
+  // 'loadstart' is queued just before the media element starts attaching to
+  // the MediaSource, and fires before the element's player finishes opening
+  // the MediaSource. Destroy the MediaSource's context in that window.
+  video.addEventListener('loadstart', t.step_func(() => {
+    iframe.remove();
+    assert_equals(mediaSource.readyState, 'closed',
+                  'readyState after context destruction');
+  }), {once: true});
+
+  window.addEventListener('load', t.step_func(() => {
+    assert_equals(mediaSource.readyState, 'closed',
+                  'readyState after attachment completes');
+    assert_true(isNaN(mediaSource.duration),
+                'duration after attachment completes');
+
+    // Detach the media element, which destroys its player and demuxer.
+    video.removeAttribute('src');
+    video.load();
+
+    assert_equals(mediaSource.readyState, 'closed', 'readyState after detach');
+    assert_true(isNaN(mediaSource.duration), 'duration after detach');
+    t.done();
+  }));
+
+  video.src = URL.createObjectURL(mediaSource);
+}, 'MediaSource stays closed if its context is destroyed during attachment');
+</script>
+</body>
